    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After an unforeseen failure at a key plant, the guardian of stability in the Philippines faced a significant power shortfall. Unusually high demand from the hot season squeezed the grid, but responsible stewards took protective action. They acted to prevent a wider collapse, safeguarding vital infrastructure for the community facing the crisis, even as the threat of power cuts to homes and businesses loomed.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "how-4",
          "why-2",
          "result-1",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [
        "how_fragments_expanded_to_contiguous_span"
      ],
      "fit": 0.65
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "A pattern of breakdowns across the system, including a generation unit going offline, led to a large loss of generation capacity. This, combined with peak demand conditions, strained the system. The grid management authority responded by implementing load reduction measures to prevent infrastructure damage, though the risk of rotational blackouts remained a concern for the affected geographic area.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
        "fragments": [
          "how-2",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-3",
          "result-2",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.55
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The unit tripping offline was part of prolonged outages at other plants, creating ongoing challenges in the power system. Heat pushed demand to the edge of supply, prompting a grid emergency declaration for the Visayas region. Public officials ordered load shedding to prevent line overload, an effort to manage the crisis and keep essential power flowing.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "why-1",
